From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:37:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150: CPUs' DDR votes active-only

The CPUs' path to DDR, which cpufreq votes from the OPP tables, has tag 0:
the vote goes into the sleep set as well, and since cpufreq doesn't drop it
in s2idle, it holds DDR, and CX under it, after the cluster collapses. The
SoC never reaches CXSD, AOSD or DDR sleep. With the vote active-only, as
on sm8350 and the later SoCs, the cluster's collapse takes it out, and on
flame the qcom_stats counts for all three grow in an unplugged suspend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
index c6d3f74b6a46..87579145918b 100644
